WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:02.703
I recently started a little support group,

00:00:02.703 --> 00:00:05.480
the JMA group, the Jewish
Mothers Anonymous group.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.011
(audience laughter)

00:00:07.011 --> 00:00:09.382
Last week we were talking
about weaning our sons

00:00:09.382 --> 00:00:12.198
off of breast feeding
by the age of nineteen.

00:00:12.198 --> 00:00:13.794
(audience laughter)

00:00:13.794 --> 00:00:16.294
(light music)

00:00:17.697 --> 00:00:20.247
Alright guys, so I recently
got a job at BuzzFeed

00:00:20.247 --> 00:00:22.549
and my mom, she made faces,

00:00:22.549 --> 00:00:24.735
she doesn't think it's that hard of a job

00:00:24.735 --> 00:00:25.767
she's not impressed.

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:27.762
It's an arts and crafts job

00:00:27.762 --> 00:00:28.909
that you get paid for.

00:00:28.909 --> 00:00:30.609
You have to make a video today.

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:31.926
Yes, I'm up for the challenge.

00:00:31.926 --> 00:00:33.640
You think you'll do well?
Yes, I know I will do well.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.301
And then you're going to perform stand-up.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:38.056
Okay, how many minutes?

00:00:38.056 --> 00:00:38.889
Five minutes.

00:00:38.889 --> 00:00:39.722
Five minutes?

00:00:39.722 --> 00:00:41.211
Okay, I can talk for five minutes.

00:00:41.211 --> 00:00:42.967
I'm funny, people laugh at my jokes.

00:00:42.967 --> 00:00:43.863
I kill me.

00:00:43.863 --> 00:00:45.368
Tell me one funny joke right now.

00:00:45.368 --> 00:00:46.589
So the guy goes to the pharmacist,

00:00:46.589 --> 00:00:48.563
he puts his penis on the table,

00:00:48.563 --> 00:00:49.396
puts a dollar next to his penis.

00:00:49.396 --> 00:00:50.229
Nope.

00:00:50.229 --> 00:00:51.062
Nope nope.

00:00:51.062 --> 00:00:53.223
My mom does this terrible
Seinfeld impersonation

00:00:53.223 --> 00:00:55.501
that just, she finds hilarious.

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:58.598
What's the deal with taxi cabs?

00:00:58.598 --> 00:01:00.426
(laughing)

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:01.900
I'm going to have the best time

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.328
at BuzzFeed, I think it will be just fun

00:01:04.328 --> 00:01:06.577
and exciting and interesting

00:01:06.577 --> 00:01:08.428
and the time is just gonna fly by

00:01:08.428 --> 00:01:12.345
and I'm gonna produce a
25 million views video.

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:16.600
So this is the BuzzFeed reception.

00:01:17.489 --> 00:01:20.490
Espresso mild, espresso
bold, espresso bland,

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:22.902
americano, double espresso.

00:01:22.902 --> 00:01:23.984
I had to make several coffees

00:01:23.984 --> 00:01:26.252
because this was a very
complicated process.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.623
Okay, this one is better.

00:01:27.623 --> 00:01:29.845
I don't know what to do with this one.

00:01:29.845 --> 00:01:32.150
I'm gonna trash it, carefully.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:33.468
I have to go find my safe space

00:01:33.468 --> 00:01:35.092
and be productive.

00:01:35.092 --> 00:01:37.509
This is productive workspace.

00:01:38.741 --> 00:01:40.525
It's like a (beep) dreidel.

00:01:40.525 --> 00:01:43.692
Oh my god how do I get off this chair?

00:01:49.023 --> 00:01:51.086
Alright, I think I'm ready.

00:01:51.086 --> 00:01:52.999
I'm ready for this.

00:01:52.999 --> 00:01:54.857
I can do this, I can't hear anything.

00:01:54.857 --> 00:01:56.107
I'm deaf. Whoa.

00:02:00.729 --> 00:02:01.646
It's dying.

00:02:02.741 --> 00:02:04.471
Oh here it is.

00:02:04.471 --> 00:02:06.971
Oh shit, it's under the table.

00:02:08.838 --> 00:02:10.943
This is not intended for my age group.

00:02:10.943 --> 00:02:12.299
I need a rest. I need a nap.

00:02:12.299 --> 00:02:13.647
I need lunch.

00:02:13.647 --> 00:02:14.855
So I did a little research on kind of

00:02:14.855 --> 00:02:16.724
what you guys do well,

00:02:16.724 --> 00:02:18.467
what are the good statistics.

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:21.971
And it seems that videos that
have animals in them go viral.

00:02:21.971 --> 00:02:23.886
That's true.
Right.

00:02:23.886 --> 00:02:26.982
So I was thinking, how cool would it be

00:02:26.982 --> 00:02:29.382
if we did a video where people

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:32.046
act like certain animals for a day?

00:02:32.046 --> 00:02:34.911
And you know, like I'd go like this,

00:02:34.911 --> 00:02:36.855
and like do that kind of stuff.

00:02:36.855 --> 00:02:38.467
Or like I could be a dog and go like

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:40.033
pet me pet me pet me.
Uh huh.

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:40.866
Oh yeah.

00:02:40.866 --> 00:02:42.096
So we could do rooster people,

00:02:42.096 --> 00:02:45.378
we could do a cow person, like.

00:02:45.378 --> 00:02:48.128
(sped-up speech)

00:02:49.854 --> 00:02:52.176
What has been the best
idea recently at Buzzfeed?

00:02:52.176 --> 00:02:54.318
Farts in a jar off eBay.

00:02:54.318 --> 00:02:56.416
And had people smell them, so.

00:02:56.416 --> 00:02:59.224
Maybe that, is that getting
juices going in your--

00:02:59.224 --> 00:03:00.537
I could do it without the jar.

00:03:00.537 --> 00:03:01.894
Can we do farts without the jar?

00:03:01.894 --> 00:03:03.136
Just smell farts?

00:03:03.136 --> 00:03:04.049
(laughing)

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:05.004
People smell farts?

00:03:05.004 --> 00:03:06.849
Maybe we can do a video where

00:03:06.849 --> 00:03:08.800
you try to recognize your relatives

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.496
by the smell of the fart.

00:03:11.496 --> 00:03:12.329
This is very challenging.

00:03:12.329 --> 00:03:14.083
I need to actually find people to film

00:03:14.083 --> 00:03:16.805
in this ridiculous video that I'm doing.

00:03:16.805 --> 00:03:17.805
Excuse me.

00:03:20.762 --> 00:03:25.187
I'm looking for a cast,
for guys who can recognize

00:03:25.187 --> 00:03:28.509
the farts, or girls, of
their significant others.

00:03:28.509 --> 00:03:29.483
Oh.

00:03:29.483 --> 00:03:32.629
Would you be willing to be my cast?

00:03:32.629 --> 00:03:34.111
He's married.
He's married?

00:03:34.111 --> 00:03:35.874
So he should definitely
be able to help you out.

00:03:35.874 --> 00:03:37.321
No?

00:03:37.321 --> 00:03:38.470
You know I hate to admit it,

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:40.175
this was not as easy as I thought.

00:03:40.175 --> 00:03:42.490
I got my idea approved, so that was good,

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:44.144
I got to that point,
but then the equipment

00:03:44.144 --> 00:03:46.264
completely threw me off.

00:03:46.264 --> 00:03:48.963
So I'm gonna focus on my stand-up routine.

00:03:48.963 --> 00:03:52.914
So that I can at least succeed
in one part of this task.

00:03:52.914 --> 00:03:54.321
Here's the thing at comedy mic.

00:03:54.321 --> 00:03:55.812
We really just want to be

00:03:55.812 --> 00:03:57.471
the most supportive mic in New York City.

00:03:57.471 --> 00:03:58.543
(beep), it's a full house.

00:03:58.543 --> 00:04:01.738
I was not envisioning a real place,

00:04:01.738 --> 00:04:03.825
I thought that this was going to be staged

00:04:03.825 --> 00:04:06.874
and scripted, and it's (beep) not.

00:04:06.874 --> 00:04:08.696
And there's like real people in there.

00:04:08.696 --> 00:04:12.080
Our next comic is making her comedy debut.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:12.913
(audience applause)

00:04:12.913 --> 00:04:16.246
Give it up for Irine Tabach everybody.

00:04:18.953 --> 00:04:19.786
Hi guys.

00:04:20.638 --> 00:04:22.838
Yeah, I have to figure this out.

00:04:22.838 --> 00:04:24.511
How do you use this?

00:04:24.511 --> 00:04:26.630
My son came out to me.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:28.273
This is still a little
sensitive, you know,

00:04:28.273 --> 00:04:29.877
I'm from the old country,

00:04:29.877 --> 00:04:31.626
a different generation,

00:04:31.626 --> 00:04:33.517
totally different upbringing.

00:04:33.517 --> 00:04:35.232
He sat me down and told me that he's

00:04:35.232 --> 00:04:37.156
not going to medical school.

00:04:37.156 --> 00:04:40.082
(audience laughter)

00:04:40.082 --> 00:04:43.774
So my son took me to take
your parent to work day.

00:04:43.774 --> 00:04:45.871
I kid you not, they have that at BuzzFeed.

00:04:45.871 --> 00:04:49.102
It was like a really cool
daycare for older kids.

00:04:49.102 --> 00:04:51.123
(audience laughter)

00:04:51.123 --> 00:04:53.574
Yeah, they do arts and
crafts projects all day

00:04:53.574 --> 00:04:54.775
and they get paid for it.

00:04:54.775 --> 00:04:58.166
(audience laughter)

00:04:58.166 --> 00:05:00.976
Everything free, free coffee, free candy,

00:05:00.976 --> 00:05:03.309
free massages, free alcohol,

00:05:04.278 --> 00:05:06.527
play room, game rooms.

00:05:06.527 --> 00:05:09.217
You know, I grew up in
the former Soviet Union

00:05:09.217 --> 00:05:11.726
but I found communism at BuzzFeed.

00:05:11.726 --> 00:05:14.726
(audience laughter)

00:05:16.811 --> 00:05:19.521
Okay, that was pretty impressive mom.

00:05:19.521 --> 00:05:21.806
I was very surprised with myself.

00:05:21.806 --> 00:05:23.376
Actually, people laughed.

00:05:23.376 --> 00:05:24.620
Have you learned anything from today?

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:26.420
I've learned that my son actually

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:28.414
has a very challenging job

00:05:28.414 --> 00:05:30.838
producing these viral videos.

00:05:30.838 --> 00:05:33.186
These guys are very talented.

00:05:33.186 --> 00:05:34.951
- [Eric] My mom's got a
new special coming out

00:05:34.951 --> 00:05:36.011
on Netflix, it's called--

00:05:36.011 --> 00:05:37.678
- [Irine] I kill me.

